      "extract_value": "The conclusion reports that online appearance-focused experiences among adolescent girls are negatively associated with intuitive eating, while broad conceptualizations of beauty and body appreciation are positively associated with intuitive eating. It suggests that interventions that broaden concepts of beauty and increase body appreciation may help facilitate positive eating behaviors. The section does not reference any study identifiers, sample characteristics, methods, or numerical statistics.",
      "evidence_source": "The online context, in which most adolescent girls engage daily, presents the impression that others focus most on girls' external appearance. Unfortunately, the present study finds such experiences to be negatively associated with intuitive eating. However, because broad conceptualization of beauty and body appreciation are positively associated with intuitive eating, broadening conceptualization of beauty and increasing body appreciation in future intervention programs may help to facilitate positive eating behaviors.",
